-- title:
--   Arbitrarily deep levels: Frobenius order divisible by n
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime number and let $\varphi$ be an element of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q/\mathbb{Q}_q)$, the group of $\mathbb{Q}_q$-algebra automorphisms of the fixed algebraic closure `PadicAlgCl q`. Write $r$ for the homomorphism `primeLocalToGlobal q`, which restricts scalars to $\mathbb{Q}$ and then restricts the resulting automorphism to the normal subextension $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and let $A$ be the valuation subring `primeLocalPlace q` of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, the pullback of $\mathbb{Z}_q\subset\mathbb{Q}_q$ along the chosen embedding. Assume $r(\varphi)$ is a Frobenius element at $A$ for the exponent $q$: it lies in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and acts on the residue field of $A$ by $x\mapsto x^{q}$. Let $F_0$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ of finite degree over $\mathbb{Q}$, and let $n$ be a positive natural number. Then there is an intermediate field $F$ with $F_0\le F$, again of finite degree over $\mathbb{Q}$, such that for every natural number $j$: if $\varphi^{j}$ lies in the subgroup of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q/\mathbb{Q}_q)$ generated by $r^{-1}$ of the inertia subgroup of $A$ (taken inside $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ as the image of the inertia subgroup under the inclusion of the decomposition subgroup) together with $r^{-1}$ of the subgroup fixing $F$ pointwise, then $n$ divides $j$.
--
--   This is the existence of unramified levels of arbitrary depth at $q$: the residue degree at the chosen place of a finite level $F$, equivalently the order of the image of Frobenius in the finite quotient of the local Galois group by inertia together with the fixing subgroup of $F$, can be made divisible by any prescribed $n$ by enlarging $F$. It is used in the computation of the dimension of the unramified part of $H^1$ at $q$ in terms of invariants, and in the associated vanishing statements for local classes.
